msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:122
#. Diagram label
msgid "Task complete?"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:172
#. Diagram label
msgid "Task logged"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The only lane in this diagram that chooses: one entry by id, or everything. It was split out from a single conflated lane because a person's choice and a scheduled sweep's fixed program are not the same actor, which is why the sweep below has a lane of its own rather than sharing this one."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:179
#. Diagram label
msgid "The periodic sweep fires"
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:112
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The task itself. This diagram says nothing about how it is done; it only brackets it, so that a reader of the log can tell where one run of work began and ended."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "What an agent writes down about its own run, and what a person can do with it afterwards: task starts and ends, messages and errors, persisted where somebody can read them. You are in this process on every task, whether or not capture is on — the first gateway is what decides, and an agent that does not check it logs into nothing. The log operator's lane is the other half: a person discards one entry or a whole session, and the scheduled sweep does neither on its own. This is not the work plan. `beans` records WHAT is being worked on and survives the session; this records what happened during it. The two answer different questions and a reader reaching for one is badly served by the other."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:123
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Which way the work goes after it."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:127
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write a message or error entry whenever a later reader would need it. A command run goes in `execution` (command, exit code, where output went) — never the output itself, and never a secret, token or credential: capture on puts entries in git."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:137
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write a task-end entry, with the outcome in the detail. The step is the unit: an entry per step, not one when the whole process finishes, or every intermediate entry is lost."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:102
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Write a task-start entry before touching anything: summary, actor, and the process/task/bean/branch/session it belongs to where they exist. role, process and task are optional on purpose — do not invent a lane for work done outside a process."
msgstr ""

#: sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn:226
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
